# SPA fallback for client routes that are NOT prerendered to static HTML.
# `/` is the index document; `/blog` and `/blog/<slug>` are prerendered files
# (served directly). `/contact` is the only client route needing the shell.
# NOTE: add any NEW non-prerendered client route here, or it will 404 on direct load.
/contact    /index.html    200

# Anything else that isn't a real file/prerendered page → a real 404 (not a
# soft-404). 404.html is noindex, so bogus URLs never get indexed.
/*          /404.html      404
